From 20feda27bdc03113b105b9d962b2c86dee1ba8aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:10:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Measure V3 plan yield across history: the shortfall is
 chronic

Replayed six sessions spanning Nov 2025 to Aug 2026 to test whether V3's
one-tradeable-plan-per-day was a bad session or its normal behaviour.

It is normal.

  date        regime    evaluated  plans
  2025-11-03  NEUTRAL           0      0   (no symbol had 260 sessions yet)
  2026-02-02  BEAR            568      0
  2026-03-16  BEAR            589      0
  2026-05-04  NEUTRAL         682      0
  2026-06-15  NEUTRAL         698      0
  2026-07-16  NEUTRAL         734      2
  2026-08-20  NEUTRAL         759      1

Across the five usable sessions: 3,271 candidates evaluated, 2 carried an entry,
stop and target. A rate of 0.06 per cent. Four of five sessions produced none at
all.

Classifications across all sessions: REJECT 2,592 / WATCH 677 / ACTION 2.

So V3 is not under-recording -- it is barely producing anything to record. Its
weekly relative-strength discovery works and ranks hundreds of names, but by the
time it confirms, the great majority are either WEAK or already EXTENDED, and
the daily trigger finds no valid entry structure. On 2026-08-20 that was 170 of
192 WATCH candidates with NO_TRIGGER and 150 already extended.

This also explains the empty portfolio: with roughly half a plan per session
since go-live on 2026-08-04, near-zero committed capital is the expected outcome,
not a persistence defect.

Adds resume support to the replay script so a multi-month run can proceed a few
sessions at a time, and corrects the trigger-key lookup, which read metrics
rather than the candidate payload and reported '?' for every row.
---
 scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py b/scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py
index a5763e4..00c090c 100755
--- a/scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py
+++ b/scripts/replay_v3_plan_yield.py
@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ def replay_date(
             continue
         classes[str(candidate.classification)] += 1
         plan_states[str(candidate.metrics.get("trade_plan_state", "?"))] += 1
-        triggers[str(candidate.metrics.get("setup", "?"))] += 1
+        triggers[str(getattr(candidate, "setup", None)
+                      or candidate.metrics.get("entry_trigger")
+                      or candidate.metrics.get("setup", "?"))] += 1
         timings[str(candidate.metrics.get("timing_state", "?"))] += 1
         # A tradeable plan is the only thing that can become a position.
         if candidate.classification == "ACTION" and float(candidate.entry or 0) > 0:
@@ -176,9 +178,21 @@ def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
         targets = targets[:args.limit]
     print(f"replaying {len(targets)} session(s): {targets[0]} .. {targets[-1]}", flush=True)
 
-    results = []
     out = Path(args.out)
     out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    # Resume-friendly: a long replay may be run a few sessions at a time.
+    results = []
+    if out.exists():
+        try:
+            results = json.loads(out.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
+            done = {r.get("date") for r in results}
+            targets = [d for d in targets if d not in done]
+            print(f"resuming: {len(results)} session(s) already recorded, "
+                  f"{len(targets)} remaining", flush=True)
+        except (ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError):
+            results = []
+    if not targets:
+        print("nothing left to replay")
     for index, date in enumerate(targets, start=1):
         t0 = time.time()
         try:
@@ -197,6 +211,8 @@ def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
               f"  regime={row.get('regime', '-')}  ({time.time() - t0:.0f}s)", flush=True)
         out.write_text(json.dumps(results, indent=2, default=str), encoding="utf-8")
 
+    results.sort(key=lambda r: str(r.get("date")))
+    out.write_text(json.dumps(results, indent=2, default=str), encoding="utf-8")
     plans = [r.get("tradeable_plans", 0) for r in results if "tradeable_plans" in r]
     if plans:
         print("\n" + "=" * 58)
